<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">22 June in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 22 June, from 217 BCE to 1944.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/ptolemy-iv-philopator" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ptolemy-iv-philopator.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/217-bce">217 BCE</a> <span class="tih-ago">2,242 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ptolemy IV defeats Antiochus III at the Battle of Raphia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ptolemy-iv-philopator">Ptolemy IV Philopator</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> defeated the Seleucid king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antiochus-iii-the-great">Antiochus III the Great</a> near present-day Rafah in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fourth-syrian-war">Fourth Syrian War</a>, with native Egyptian troops playing a significant role. The battle determined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coele-syria">Coele-Syria</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-raphia">Battle of Raphia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ptolemy-iv-philopator">Ptolemy IV Philopator</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antiochus-iii-the-great">Antiochus III the Great</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/168-bce">168 BCE</a> <span class="tih-ago">2,193 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Rome defeats Macedon at Pydna</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lucius-aemilius-paullus-macedonicus">Lucius Aemilius Paullus</a>'s legions broke the Macedonian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phalanx">phalanx</a> of King Perseus. The Antigonid kingdom was abolished, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> became the dominant power in the Greek world.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">813 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,213 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Khan Krum routs the Byzantine army at Versinikia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krum">Khan Krum</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> routed the Byzantine army of Emperor Michael I Rangabe near Versinikia, not far from Adrianople in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thrace">Thrace</a>. The defeat led to Michael's overthrow in favour of Leo V the Armenian, and Krum went on to besiege Adrianople.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-versinikia">Battle of Versinikia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krum">Krum</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">816 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,210 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Stephen IV is elected pope after the death of Leo III</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Stephen IV, of a noble Roman family, was elected pope after the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-leo-iii">Pope Leo III</a> earlier in June. In October he crowned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-pious">Louis the Pious</a> as emperor at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reims">Reims</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-leo-iii">Pope Leo III</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1633">1633 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">393 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Galileo is made to abjure before the Inquisition</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Found 'vehemently suspect of heresy', <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galileo-galilei">Galileo</a> formally abjured the view that the Earth moves around the Sun. He spent the rest of his life under house arrest.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1772">1772 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">254 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Lord Mansfield rules in the Somerset case</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The judge held that James <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somerset">Somerset</a>, an enslaved man brought to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, could not be forcibly removed abroad. The ruling was widely taken to mean <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> had no basis in English law.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1941">1941 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">85 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Germany invades the Soviet Union</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/operation-barbarossa">Operation Barbarossa</a> sent some three million <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/axis-powers">Axis</a> troops across a front from the Baltic to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a>. The war in the east became the largest and deadliest land conflict in history.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1944">1944 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">82 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Roosevelt signs the G.I. Bill</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Servicemen's Readjustment Act gave veterans college tuition, low-cost home loans and unemployment pay. Millions took up its benefits, expanding higher education and home ownership.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 22 June <span class="n">7</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/emperor-ruizong-of-tang"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/emperor-ruizong-of-tang.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Emperor Ruizong of Tang</span><span class="tp">662–716</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/sayf-al-dawla"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Sayf al-Dawla</span><span class="tp">916–967</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/wilhelm-von-humboldt"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/wilhelm-von-humboldt.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Wilhelm von Humboldt</span><span class="tp">1767–1835</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/giuseppe-mazzini"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/giuseppe-mazzini.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Giuseppe Mazzini</span><span class="tp">1805–1872</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/richard-seddon"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/richard-seddon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Richard Seddon</span><span class="tp">1845–1906</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/h-rider-haggard"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/h-rider-haggard.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">H. Rider Haggard</span><span class="tp">1856–1925</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/soraya-esfandiary-bakhtiary"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/soraya-esfandiary-bakhtiary.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Soraya Esfandiary-Bakhtiary</span><span class="tp">1932–2001</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 22 June <span class="n">2</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/gebhard-duke-of-lotharingia"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Gebhard, Duke of Lotharingia</span><span class="tp">d. 910</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/roger-i-of-sicily"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/roger-i-of-sicily.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Roger I of Sicily</span><span class="tp">c. 1031–1101</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
